From k43. Git::Native (Remote.pm, _pushurl) and App::karr both look up git_remote_pushurl locally through Git::Libgit2::FFI::ffi()->function, because Git::Libgit2 does not bind it. git-native-core names a second distribution needing the same function as the threshold for a binding in Git::Libgit2; that threshold is now reached.

Open decision for the maintainer, no commitment: bind it in Git::Libgit2 (then pin that version here and drop the local lookup), or keep the local lookups. Returns a string, no rc; NULL is undef.

Cross-repo: filed on the Git::Libgit2 board as its card 23. Nothing to do here until that lands and a Git::Libgit2 version is released (the release waits for the maintainer); then pin it and drop the local attach in Remote.pm.
